{
  "step_by_step_reasoning": "1. External actors: UserConsumerWeb uploads video content into S3.\n2. S3 triggers Step Functions to orchestrate media processing.\n3. Step Functions invokes Elemental MediaConvert (transcoding/proxy creation), Rekognition (video metadata/celebrity/content identification), and Transcribe (audio-to-text conversion).\n4. MediaConvert and Rekognition output metadata into DynamoDB.\n5. Transcribe sends extracted text to Comprehend for analysis, which then outputs its results to DynamoDB.\n6. DynamoDB acts as a temporary metadata store, ingested by the Reach Engine platform running on EC2 and EKS.",
